\p
\v 1 Then¦112260 Yahweh's¦112263 messenger¦112261 went from¦112264 Gilgal¦112266 to¦112267 Bokim¦112269 and¦112271 told¦112271 \add the Israelis\add*, “I¦112272 brought¦112272 you¦112273 all out of Egypt¦112274 and¦112275 led you¦112276 here to¦112277 this land¦112279 that¦112280 I¦112281 promised¦112281 to¦112282 your¦112282 ancestors¦112282. I¦112283 had said¦112283 that I¦112286 wouldn't ever break¦112286 my¦112287 agreement¦112287 with¦112288 you¦112288 all,
\v 2 but¦112291 that you mustn't form treaties¦112295 with the¦112296 peoples who lived¦112296 here, rather you¦112300 must¦112300 tear¦112300 down¦112300 their¦112299 altars¦112299.\x + \xo 2:2: \xt Exo 34:12-13; Deu 7:2-5.\x* But¦112301 you¦112303 all haven't obeyed¦112303 what I said. What have¦112308 you¦112308 \add gone and\add* done¦112308?
